{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>ורדפה</b> — The one who says that the dalet has a dagesh, for so is every thing that is continual, which a man engages in and has no end — perhaps this grammarian will explain to us what the difference is between הדובר בי and רוח ה׳ דבר בי, הנני גורש מפניך, לא אגרשנו, ויגרש את האדם. These forms are found in the binyan kal and in the binyan kaved, and many like this. And the correct view is that the kal of רדף is always after the one who flees, and the word ירדף חשך goes out to two agents, and likewise ורדפה את מאהביה — that she will pursue after them when they flee from her." "<b>ובקשתם</b> — Missing dagesh in the qof, for it is from the binyan kaved, and likewise שלחו באש מקדשך — to lighten upon the tongue, therefore these are missing dagesh."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:11.081244547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}